iled only  Change-Id: Ia61233542a9b86d9ee9ab7da52f0eca5cc271512 Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/401283 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="401283" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/83/401283/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="6"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5dde540ad96acacebca20f1151806e2f1d490907" commit="f9b3b971fea19ad2779e4032d2ba478c1a10e210" commit_message="Add bluetoothauto dependency to control file  BUG:b:33103359 Change-Id: I5dde540ad96acacebca20f1151806e2f1d490907 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414274 Commit-Ready: Tom Turney &lt;tturney@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Tom Turney &lt;tturney@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Benjamin Peake &lt;bpeake@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tom Turney &lt;tturney@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414274" owner_email="tturney@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/74/414274/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id75b5efc658b3dbae26dd3037c795c6bc28a91a7" commit="6f6c6edf77542c98085f37b82e89b9360529e044" commit_message="ec-utils: remove build products before running make  When ec-utils 9999 ebuild is emerged, the entire contents of the local tree is copied into the sandbox.  If the local tree contains built images, make invoked by ebuild reports that the target is up to date. This is very harmful when board the ebuild is invoked for is not an x86 board: the generated image is include in the root file system, but it is not executable on the target.  Invoking 'make clean' first makes sure that the image is rebuilt.  BUG=none TEST=proper executable for gru is generated even when prebuilt      usb_updater for x86 exists.  Change-Id: Id75b5efc658b3dbae26dd3037c795c6bc28a91a7 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414308 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="414308" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/08/414308/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I7189a1637c8cd5aeb9727ebc09263e90b3b96524" commit="af656b42a009635aa3988cb76a4245a3eedac455" commit_message="CHROMIUM: video/tegra: nvmap: fix nvmap create handle vulnerability  Handle the race condition between malicious fd close and copy_to_user error, which can create use after free condition. This is fixed by deferring the fd install, which eliminates the race that leads to use after free condition.  This patch fixes a security vulnerability reported here: https://code.google.com/p/android/issues/detail?id=225165  Change-Id: I7189a1637c8cd5aeb9727ebc09263e90b3b96524 Signed-off-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/413805 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="413805" owner_email="markz@gpartner-nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/05/413805/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="Icccca636df007f943b931f2fd0ba88f699aee221" commit="4397cde46858e3121a1928d711895722e04b7559" commit_message="CHROMIUM: video/tegra: Protect channel ioctl  Chann